        defendant: [.direct("Did you stab {V}?", "\"Yes. {V} swung a bidder paddle at me, and I pulled my pocket knife and struck out. I was afraid.\""), .direct("Why did you have a pocket knife?", "\"I carry one for work. It is a tool I use every day, and I did not bring it to a fight.\""), .direct("What was the bidding dispute about?", "\"We bid against each other all day on the same animals. It got personal, and things were said.\""), .direct("What was the dispute about?", "\"We kept bidding against each other on cattle, and {V} accused me of running up the price. We argued in the aisle.\""), .direct("What did {V} do?", "\"{V} swung the paddle at my head. I raised my arm, and then I had my knife out.\""), .direct("What did you do after?", "\"I stepped back in shock and saw blood. I called for help and stayed until deputies came.\""), .cross("The paddle had a split edge. Did it actually hit you?", "\"It came close. I did not feel it hit, but I thought it would.\""), .cross("A deep side wound is a serious injury, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not mean to hurt {V.him} that badly. It happened fast.\""), .cross("You could have walked away from a bidding dispute, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. I wish I had.\""), .cross("You carried a pocket knife to a sale, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I always do for cutting twine. I did not carry it to hurt anyone.\""), .cross("{V} was stabbed in the side, wasn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes, and the wound was deep. I did not mean it to be.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a ranch hand, was stabbed in the side in a livestock sale barn after a bidding dispute. The auctioneer says {D} had the knife, and the pocket knife was recovered with blood on it.", "The defense evidence will establish that {V} swung a bidder paddle with a split edge at {D}, and that {D} used a pocket knife in fear."),
        closings: ("A bidding dispute, a pocket knife with blood on it, and a deep wound in {V}'s side. The auctioneer saw the knife in {D}'s hand, and nobody else had one.", "A bidder paddle with a split edge swung in a crowded barn, and a split-second reaction. The State must prove {D} was not defending {D.himself} from it."),
