        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Friend", "{DL} says {D.he} was visiting a friend.")],
        role: "Fire investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role in this case?", "\"I'm a fire investigator with the county. I was called to the church school annex on {DATE} to determine where the fire started and what fed it.\""), .direct("What did you find when you examined the building?", "\"The annex, a one-story classroom building, was heavily burned. The worst damage was along the back wall, and the origin traced to the rear windows.\""), .direct("What did your testing show at the back windows?", "\"Samples from the sill and the floor beneath tested positive for an ignitable liquid, consistent with a petroleum accelerant. Pour patterns ran along the wall and under the window frames.\""), .direct("Was there any accidental source nearby?", "\"I checked the electrical panel, the heating unit, and the outlets. None were near the origin, and none showed arcing or failure that could explain a fire there.\""), .direct("What did the street camera show?", "\"{D}'s car passing and then parked near the annex at about 1 a.m. A neighbor also reported a car idling nearby before the fire.\""), .direct("How does that fit with the fire timeline?", "\"Crews were called at about 2 a.m. and were on scene by three. A fire with accelerant at the windows would spread quickly in that time.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} at the annex?", "\"No one reported seeing {D} get out of the car. The camera shows the car, not a person near the building.\""), .cross("Could the accelerant have been something used for another purpose?", "\"Possibly. Lighter fluid and similar products are common. I can only say the sample was an ignitable liquid, not who bought it.\""), .cross("Was the neighbor sure it was {D}'s car?", "\"The neighbor described a car idling. The neighbor did not read a plate or name a driver. The street camera is what ties the car to {D}.\""), .cross("Did you find any container at the scene?", "\"No can, bottle, or rag was recovered from the debris. The fire destroyed whatever might have been there.\""), .cross("How long was {D}'s car at that location?", "\"The camera shows it there for several minutes at 1 a.m. I cannot say when it left or what happened between.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Friend",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We met through our church choir years ago and have stayed close ever since. I visit {D}'s apartment often, and {D} comes by mine most weeks for dinner.\""), .direct("Were you with {D} the night of {DATE}?", "\"Yes, for part of the evening. {D} came to my apartment around nine and stayed until a little before one.\""), .direct("What did you do that evening?", "\"Mostly talked. {D} was upset about being dismissed from the school, and I tried to cheer {D} up with dinner and a movie.\""), .direct("How did {D} seem?", "\"Down, but not angry in a scary way. {D} cried at one point and said how much {D.he} missed the kids.\""), .direct("When did {D} leave?", "\"Just before one, I believe. I walked {D} to the door and watched the car leave.\""), .direct("Does {D} cook out often?", "\"Yes. {D} grills on the patio most weekends and has a charcoal grill I have eaten from many times.\""), .cross("Did you see where {D} went after leaving?", "\"No. I closed the door and went to bed. I can't say where {D} drove.\""), .cross("Did {D} mention the annex?", "\"Not that night. {D} spent the whole evening talking about the dismissal, the other teachers, and how much {D.he} missed the children in the classroom.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything about wanting revenge?", "\"No. I never heard {D} talk about getting even with anyone. {D} was sad and tired that night, the kind of tired that comes after crying.\""), .cross("How far is your apartment from the annex?", "\"About ten minutes by car. It sits on the road {D} takes home, so driving past that corner would be perfectly normal for {D}.\""), .cross("Do you know whether {D} made a call before going home?", "\"I don't know. {D} might have called someone from the car, but I was already inside my apartment by then, so I can only guess.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned an annex.", "A friend visit."),
