        truths: ("{DL} bought lighter fluid that week.", "{DL} grills often."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you near the annex at 1 a.m.?", "\"I was driving back from a friend's apartment on that side of town. I stopped on the street to take a phone call before I went home.\""), .direct("Did you work at the school?", "\"Yes, as a teacher until a week earlier. I was dismissed after a dispute, and I was angry and hurt about it.\""), .direct("Did you start the fire?", "\"No. I did not go near the building. I never got out of my car, and I would never put children's classrooms at risk.\""), .direct("Why did you buy lighter fluid that week?", "\"I grill on my patio most weekends. I picked up a can at the hardware store with my groceries. It had nothing to do with the school.\""), .direct("Where did you go after the call?", "\"Home, which is about fifteen minutes away. I fell asleep and woke to a message about the fire.\""), .direct("What would you say about the children?", "\"I taught those children. I would never hurt them or their classroom, and I'm heartbroken they lost it.\""), .cross("You were dismissed a week before the fire, weren't you?", "\"Yes. It was a painful dismissal, and I won't pretend otherwise. It does not mean I would burn the building.\""), .cross("Your car was on the street camera at 1 a.m., wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I have never said it wasn't. I was parked there for a call.\""), .cross("You bought lighter fluid that same week, didn't you?", "\"I did, for my grill. I can't prove that, except that I grill often and my neighbors know it.\""), .cross("You never told anyone you were at the annex until deputies asked, did you?", "\"No. I had no reason to. I didn't know there had been a fire until later.\""), .cross("You parked close to the building, didn't you?", "\"I was parked on the street nearby, which is where I always park on that block. It is the spot I used the whole time I worked at the school.\"")],
        openings: ("A church school annex burned overnight, and accelerant was found at the back windows. {D}, a teacher dismissed a week earlier, was on the street camera near the annex at 1 a.m., a car was idling nearby, and {D} had bought lighter fluid that week. The fire investigator will describe the burn.", "{D} was driving home from a friend's apartment and stopped to take a call. A friend will tell you {D} was grieving the dismissal, not planning anything, and that {D} grills most weekends. No one saw {D} near the building."),
        closings: ("Accelerant at the back windows, a dismissed teacher with a grudge, a car on the camera at 1 a.m., and lighter fluid bought that week. The children lost their classroom. These facts point in one direction.", "No one saw {D} leave the car, no container was recovered, and lighter fluid is sold at every hardware store. {D} grills often and spent the evening with a friend. The State must prove {D} lit the fire."),
        timeline: [(-7, "{DL} is dismissed."), (0, "1 a.m.: the car."), (0, "2 a.m.: the fire."), (0, "3 a.m.: crews.")],
        identified: "A fire report.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a weapon"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "The children lost their classroom.",
        doctrines: ["alibi"])

